    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nBefore `mini.completion`, I've used `nvim-cmp` and `coq-nvim` for autocompletion. On both plugins, they have a configuration for disabling autocompletion, so I could trigger it with some keybinding when needed because I don't really like the completion window popping up on my screen while I type.\r\n\r\nI've implemented and tested this feature on a local fork and it worked pretty nice. I am wondering if you guys would accept a PR from me.",
